## 1. Objective
When deployed on a website (`https://tenuto-studio-5-production.up.railway.app/`), Tenuto Studio 5 currently has three viewport and mobile usability issues:
1. **No Fullscreen Mode & `100vh`/`100vw` Overflow:** `SplitWorkspace.tsx` uses `h-screen w-screen`, which overflows mobile browser address bars, and lacks a Fullscreen toggle button (`requestFullscreen` / `webkitRequestFullscreen` + CSS fixed-viewport fallback when embedded inside an iframe or mobile Safari).
2. **Hardcoded Side-by-Side Split on Mobile (`grid-cols-2`):** `SplitWorkspace.tsx` forces `grid-cols-2` on all screen widths. On a mobile phone (`375px–430px` wide), squeezing the Monaco Code Editor and the Piano Roll side-by-side into `~185px` each makes both panes unusable, and opening the bottom dock (`h-80`) covers most of the vertical screen.
3. **Mouse-Only Piano Roll Interactions:** `WebGPUCanvas.tsx` only binds mouse events (`onMouseDown`, `mousemove`, `mouseup`) and desktop trackpad wheel zoom (`ctrlKey + wheel`), lacking mobile `touchstart` / `touchmove` / `touchend` note dragging and two-finger touch pinch-to-zoom.

This contract fixes all three issues, bumps the repository version to `5.2.2` in `package.json` and `electron-builder.json`, and updates `README.md`.

